From e0dfcdb6755753ad9f467ed1b49e1e965bf9dce8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ws07 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:33:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] Web client: NFT choice, account switches and Run states
 connected to the page's rules

- 20's NFT list (controller.loadNfts): a list not read is said as such
  (FS.nftsRead; "does not mean it has none"), never as no NFT; an answer
  for a wallet no longer connected is dropped; every wallet change reads
  it again (syncConnectedWallet).
- One reset for a new viewer (resetViewer): a wallet change, and a change
  between the wallet's own Citizen and one of its resident NFTs (nft-login,
  nft-logout). The latter keeps the wallet's key session and prize; the
  NFT played and the list belong to the wallet.
- The away summary keeps an NFT resident's marks apart from its wallet's
  (app.mjs awayWho), and its words say "wallet (or resident NFT)".
- Agent page: each sent action's state is 04's (GET /f/agent/fate, seven
  states through hud/statusview.mjs sendView; a failed read is
  "unqueryable"); a history or agent list not read is not "nothing yet".
- Tests (no key): ws07-nft 4, ws07-agent 4, screens ws07-v17 (ja/en,
  phone/PC, reload) on fixture state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
